{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980491-was-the-triat-ever-in-balance","id":980491,"title":"Was the Triat ever \"in balance\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-02T17:27:43-07:00","id":980491,"title":"Was the Triat ever \"in balance\"?","content":"Was the triat ever really in balance. Reading through the ananasi, mokole and rokea tribe books, the idea seems more and more far-fetched. For instance, in the ananasi book(ananasa's description of the fall of the weaver and the wyrm), how was the weaver(a creature of order, preservation, and perfection) able to destroy the moth fera despite her nature(that would be like the wyrm suddenly creating a non-evil race of fera from nothing), how was the weaver even capable of trapping the wyrm(a being whose sole role and existence is based around destroying the things that the weaver and wyld make), and if gaia was created by the triat how is she above/equal to them as the fera see her?<br /> <br /> Not to mention how the triats actions and abilities won't make sense when looked at critically(not helped by the spirits as they try to explain situations when they only understand them &quot;symbolically&quot;).<br /> <br /> For instance, how can the wyrm seduce/corrupt when it concept is supposedly death/entropy/destruction/purification(oddly enough, but if you think about it, it's original role was supposedly to balance the other two as the garou understand it). Wouldn't that be a more &quot;Wyld&quot;(triatic spirit of change/possibility/power/chaos) thing? or a weaver(triatic spirit of beaty/perfection/immortality/control) thing? They both fit the concept and do so regularly(the weavers one-song and drones, the wyld's random creations and gorgons), but the wyrm really doesn't have anything that would seem to fit the bill.<br /> <br /> WTA loves to avoid this by going on about how the triat is incomprehensible and alien, but they still represent predictable/well known forces of nature and many times that act outside of what there nature should be able to do. How? Are they really what the fera think they are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T18:14:30-07:00","id":980504,"title":"","content":"I think that the idea is that the Triat balance is cyclical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T18:29:40-07:00","id":980508,"title":"","content":"Prefect balance no, relative harmony maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T06:17:19-07:00","id":980726,"title":"","content":"Every member of the triat is strong. The Garou, and gaia, are just biased. They hate the wyrm not because it consumes, but because they don't want to be consumed. A deer doesn't wanna get eaten, it just wants to breed and eat and thrive. The wyrm is unpopular with most gaian spirits. Most people understandably don't want to support rape and pestilence, even though they both have uses, and you can argue that they're more wyld spirits than wyrm in some cases. The weaver didn't actually strangle the wyrm and the wyrm didn't change to get around that, rather, the weaver created a system that favours the new kind of wyrm and denies the 'old' wyrm better. Meanwhile, wyld spirits are mistaken for the other two kinds. The Wyld is thriving in the information age, and new creatures will evolve for any changing climate brought about by the wyrm. They will always perfectly be in balance (barring the universe ending), they just grow bigger as the age grows to have more in it. The old &quot;ballance wyrm&quot; is only favoured by the garou because it's simpler, they're wolves, and they can deal with it. With the current wyrm, they're just trying to make it seem more complex than it actually is, to justify their failings, when really, they haven't failed, and are probably the ones doing the worst in keeping ballance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T11:52:08-07:00","id":980919,"title":"","content":"I am not sure I entirely agree with Flower, but the idea that the Triatic balance is probably questionable. I would say the issue is harmony with Gaia, the Weaver and Wyrm have proven to be greater threats to her currently, but the wyld could just swap things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:48:18-07:00","id":981136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980491-was-the-triat-ever-in-balance?p=980726#post980726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every member of the triat is strong. The Garou, and gaia, are just biased. They hate the wyrm not because it consumes, but because they don't want to be consumed. A deer doesn't wanna get eaten, it just wants to breed and eat and thrive. The wyrm is unpopular with most gaian spirits. Most people understandably don't want to support rape and pestilence, even though they both have uses, and you can argue that they're more wyld spirits than wyrm in some cases. The weaver didn't actually strangle the wyrm and the wyrm didn't change to get around that, rather, the weaver created a system that favours the new kind of wyrm and denies the 'old' wyrm better. Meanwhile, wyld spirits are mistaken for the other two kinds. The Wyld is thriving in the information age, and new creatures will evolve for any changing climate brought about by the wyrm. They will always perfectly be in balance (barring the universe ending), they just grow bigger as the age grows to have more in it. The old &quot;ballance wyrm&quot; is only favoured by the garou because it's simpler, they're wolves, and they can deal with it. With the current wyrm, they're just trying to make it seem more complex than it actually is, to justify their failings, when really, they haven't failed, and are probably the ones doing the worst in keeping ballance.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all extremely unsupported by everything in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:52:20-07:00","id":981141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980491-was-the-triat-ever-in-balance?p=981136#post981136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is all extremely unsupported by everything in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>to be honest, very little is supported by the books. White-wolf's habit of leaving story up to the storyteller also means there is no &quot;One Truth&quot; supported by cannon, only small interpretations of everyone's best guess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:06:13-07:00","id":981150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980491-was-the-triat-ever-in-balance?p=981136#post981136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is all extremely unsupported by everything in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just my fun with Heresy. It's as Prometheas says. A lot of the stuff in the books is misinformation, or at least not the objective truth. Most factions have an interest in you using their point of view. I could possibly interpret, for example, that spirits forming broods is dodgy thing where the ones at the top of the pyramid profit from the labours of those lower down. Pledging yourself to a tribe is really just putting yourself into a slavery and isn't altogether entirely discimilar to a person pledging themselves to the infernal. That's why you've got petty shit like Pegasus VS fenrir, or the distinct probability that Griffin would try and murder anyone who tries to reform the white howlers, because he likes lion under him rather than to the side of him. If it weren't for this, they should all be working together Really, Tribal totems are just clever bastards, and you're willing pawns to them. You're fighting the wyrm not because Gaia said so, but because these spirits claim that Gaia said so. <br /> <br /> But I just like Heresy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:14:22-07:00","id":981154,"title":"","content":"There's heresy, and then there's a deconstruction with a metatextual vendetta against the genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:45:38-07:00","id":981745,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have to agree. It is pretty clear that the Wyrm and Weaver are both insane (I am not sure if the idea of sanity cannot apply to the Wyld). Gaia seeks balance, but the insanity of the Triat interferes with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T01:58:24-07:00","id":982018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980491-was-the-triat-ever-in-balance?p=981745#post981745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I have to agree. It is pretty clear that the Wyrm and Weaver are both insane (I am not sure if the idea of sanity cannot apply to the Wyld). Gaia seeks balance, but the insanity of the Triat interferes with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is more were they ever sane? There doesn't seem to be a point in Earth history that could be the case, even if you use the Shen cycle of ages the only time the world was in perfect balance was when all were one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:26:06-07:00","id":982136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980491-was-the-triat-ever-in-balance?p=982018#post982018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is more were they ever sane? There doesn't seem to be a point in Earth history that could be the case, even if you use the Shen cycle of ages the only time the world was in perfect balance was when all were one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was technically a vast, unfathomable amount of time. And is taken differently by different games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}